## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/timeloop.html
- Summary (EN): Repeats a range of frames from its input to create a looping animation. It can also blend the input over time so the wrap point is less visible.
- Résumé (FR) : Ce nœud répète une plage d'images de sa source pour créer une animation bouclée, avec un mode Cycle, Zig-Zag ou Blend pour masquer la jointure.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the VDB, Layer or Attribute to loop."]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Signature", "meaning": "The layer type the source accepts."}, {"name": "Frame Start", "meaning": "Frame where the loop begins. Output frame numbers match input frame numbers."}, {"name": "Frame Length", "meaning": "Number of frames in the loop."}, {"name": "Loop Type", "meaning": "Cycle jumps back to the start frame. Zig-Zag plays backwards at the end. Blend mixes in a copy offset by half the length."}, {"name": "Blend Shape", "meaning": "Used with Blend. Linear gives a harsh sawtooth pattern, Cosine gives a smooth curve."}]

- Caveats: ["The output keeps the input frame numbering. To start the output at frame 1, the page suggests a Time Shift COP.", "Zig-Zag is seamless, but the reversal of time is obvious.", "Cycle gives a clean loop only if the source already loops seamlessly."]

